  "verbalization": "Irbesartan is shown to interact with Cyp2d6 through a series of mechanistic pathways that ultimately involve the enzyme Cyp2d6. The evidence suggests that Irbesartan binds to Cyp2c8, which then participates in the aromatase activity, a process that Cyp2d6 also participates in. This creates a chain of interactions where Irbesartan indirectly influences Cyp2d6 through its effect on Cyp2c8. Similarly, Irbesartan's binding to Cyp1a2 leads to participation in aromatase activity, which is also a function of Cyp2d6. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Irbesartan may modulate Cyp2d6 activity, though the exact nature of this modulation remains to be fully elucidated. The integrated evidence supports a plausible, though indirect, relationship between Irbesartan and Cyp2d6, emphasizing the role of Cyp2c8 and Cyp2d6 in the metabolic pathways involving aromatase activity.",
